    "content": "## Test Summary Complete\n\nI have successfully tested all 15 checklist items for the TableSpot restaurant reservation application. Here are the results:\n\n### **PASS (13 items):**\n1. **FT-1** - Browse restaurants with full details (name, cuisine, price, rating, location, description, features)\n2. **FT-2** - Search and filter restaurants by name, cuisine, and price with conjunctive filtering\n3. **FT-3** - Create reservations with date, time, party size, and contact information\n4. **FT-4** - Cancel reservations with confirmation; cancelled reservations retained in history\n5. **FT-5** - Submit reviews with name, visit date, rating, and comment\n6. **FT-6** - Apply coupons during reservation with discount display\n7. **FT-7** - Past dates unavailable; future dates with valid times accessible\n8. **FT-8** - Modify reservation date, time, and party size with immediate updates\n9. **CS-11** - Coupon eligibility enforced (party size requirements, single coupon limit)\n10. **CS-13** - Required field validation with HTML5 error messages (name, email format, phone)\n11. **IX-14** - Modification UI provides explicit save action; cancellation requires confirmation\n12. **IX-15** - Immediate confirmation without page reload (creation, modification, cancellation)\n13. **CT-16** - Reservations display all details and distinguish Upcoming from Cancelled status\n\n### **FAIL (2 items):**\n1. **CS-10** - Review eligibility NOT enforced. App allows submitting reviews for upcoming reservations; should require completed (past) reservations only.\n2. **CT-17** - Rating inconsistency between list and detail views. Detail page rating updates (4.5→4.3) after review submission, but list view remains stale (4.8).\n\n### **Summary:**\nThe application successfully implements core reservation, review, and coupon functionality with proper UI confirmations and validation. However, there are 2 constraint/data consistency issues that should be addressed: enforcing review eligibility for completed reservations only, and syncing restaurant ratings across all views when reviews are submitted."
